        "name": "USN-6168-2",
        "description": "USN-6168-1 fixed a vulnerability in libx11. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 14.04 ESM, Ubuntu 16.04 ESM, and Ubuntu 18.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   Gregory James Duck discovered that libx11 incorrectly handled certain  Request, Event, or Error IDs. If a user were tricked into connecting to a  malicious X Server, a remote attacker could possibly use this issue to  cause libx11 to crash, resulting in a denial of service.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2023-3138"
        ]
      },
